{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778303838,"nonce":"VfHD1DqMnADr77EbdK4XaXBmcBw=","title":"EpochMaskedLoss: compositional time-mask wrapper for any AbstractLoss term","message":"Adds a compositional ``EpochMaskedLoss`` wrapper that restricts a base ``AbstractLoss`` to one or more named epochs of the trial timeline. Outside the listed epochs, the contribution is exactly zero; inside, it equals the base term computed on the masked density. The mask is built per-trial from ``trial_specs.timeline.epoch_bounds``, so it varies with per-trial randomized go-cues.\n\nSupports the three loss families currently in feedbax: ``TargetStateLoss`` (per-step), ``StateDerivativeLoss`` (cross-timestep order=1), and ``OutputJerkLoss`` (cross-timestep order=2). For cross-timestep terms, the mask is right-edge aligned — index ``i`` of the differenced array (length ``T - order``) is gated by ``mask[i + order]``, so a \"this step is in the masked set\" reading consistently penalises *outgoing* transitions.\n\nPrimary use case: suppressing pre-go anticipatory motor output without affecting post-go reach dynamics or null-space preparatory hidden activity.\n\nSurfaced from rlrmp ``efc4d68`` (smoothness retrain umbrella) anti-anticipation work on the 2026-05-09 baseline matrix. Cross-refs: ``e8f3738`` (StateDerivativeLoss), ``7e1d257`` (OutputJerkLoss), ``d67e303`` (streaming-loss extension this depends on conceptually for the `order` declaration).","files":null}]}